+## Listing TUI replay cases
+
+Use `spiral tui-replay-list` to inspect the replay catalog without running any
+cases:
+
+```console
+$ spiral tui-replay-list --filter rescue --max-cases 1
+{"version":1,"total":1,"cases":[{"id":"rescue-path","tags":["rescue","observer"]}]}
+```
+
+The command accepts `--tool-root` (or `-C`) and resolves the default
+`.spiral-coder/tui_replay.json` spec relative to that root. `--filter` performs
+an ASCII case-insensitive substring match against each case id and tag. Cases
+remain in spec order, and their tags remain in the authored order. Filtering
+happens before `--max-cases`; a zero cap is treated as one. Successful output
+contains only the version, selected-row count (`total`), and selected case ids
+and tags. An empty selection or invalid selected case is an error. Unlike
+`spiral tui-replay`, this command only lists metadata: it does not execute
+checks, call a provider, require credentials, or create replay artifacts.
+
